sections.text:
The high ones (Isa 2:11, 13) on whom the people trust, shall
be "brought low" (Isa 3:2);
therefore "cease from" depending on them, instead of on the Lord (Ps 146:3-5).

lofty city—Babylon; representative of
the stronghold of the foes of God's people in all ages (Isa 25:2, 12;
13:14).

fan—winnowed (compare Mt 3:12).

whirlwind … scatter them—(Job 27:21;
30:22).

called by my name—belong to Israel,
whose people, as sons of God, bear the name of their Father (Isa 44:5;
48:1).

for my glory—(Isa 43:21;
Isa 29:23).

(Isa 53:12; Ps 68:18;
Col 2:15).

contend with him, &c.—(Isa 54:17).
